elena: Quick FYI: our Java sample app started producing duplicate POSTs during signup when network toggles happen mid-auth. Repro on Pixel 6/7, Android 13+.

elena: Interceptor is straightforward and blocks on a synchronous token getter: 
```
class AuthInterceptor implements Interceptor {
  @Override
  public Response intercept(Chain chain) throws IOException {
    String token = TokenCache.getOrRefreshBlocking();
    Request req = chain.request().newBuilder().header("Authorization", "Bearer " + token).build();
    return chain.proceed(req);
  }
}
```

elena: Logs show the same request id enqueued twice around a connectivity change: first gets 401, token refresh starts, then another enqueue with the stale token, leading to duplicate side effects server-side.

troy: Any custom CallAdapter or custom executor for Retrofit? Also check whether TokenCache triggers network calls that reuse the same Request object.

elena: No custom adapters. We do rebuild Request each time. Key difference: the debug APK had R8/minify enabled (oops). Turning off minify for debug made the issue disappear in quick local testing.

mina: Huh. So R8 is changing the generated coroutine/bridge code timing such that dispatcher wakeups lead to a second enqueue? Short-term: disable minify in debug and add a keep rule for auth/token classes.

build-bot: CI update: debug-minified variant is part of nightly; will mark it optional and add a flaky test that toggles network for sign-in flow.

eng-runtime: FYI we shipped a tiny okhttp patch that altered dispatcher wake ordering. We'll pair on the APK to rule out client-side vs runtime interaction.

elena: Actions: 1) disable minify on debug and document it, 2) file repro with minified/non-minified APKs + logs, 3) add simple single-flight refresh wrapper in TokenCache to dedupe inflight refreshes. Filed issue: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sample-apps/issues/317

mina: Suggested temporary proguard rules: `-keep class com.redwood.sample.auth.** { *; }` and `-keepclassmembers class okhttp3.** { *; }` — narrow later.

elena: Thanks all, will follow up after pairing with eng-runtime. :thumbsup:
